  "title": "Why Ultra-Processed Foods Need Stronger Regulation",
  "summary": "Ultra-processed foods, commonly known as UPFs, have become a major part of modern diets. From packaged snacks and sugary cereals to ready meals, soft drinks and processed meat products, these foods are convenient, affordable and widely available. Their popularity is understandable, particularly for people managing busy lives. However, growing evidence about the relationship between high consumption of ultra-processed foods and poor health raises an important public policy question: should govern",
